  "body": "Follow-up of #3150 (PR #3154).\n\nPR #3154 pins `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0` and removes `CARGO_PROFILE_*` from every gate cargo call. Its proof: a second gate run on the SAME tree adds no unit directories. That holds.\n\nBut one gate run on a NEW tree still writes about 600 new unit directories under `target/debug/build/camcraft-app/<hash>/out`, each with a `libcamcraft_app-<hash>.rlib` (about 170 MB) and a `.pdb` (about 120 MB):\n- Measured on 2026-11-21 in the build worktree of the coordinator: the quick gate of PR #2920 (tree `cc04d7bcd`, which contains #3154) took `camcraft-app/` from 629 to 4386 unit directories. Free disk fell from 113 GB to 60 GB in about 3 minutes. After a sweep of the older units, the same run still holds 634 units.\n- So one revision of `camcraft-app` gets hundreds of different unit hashes in one run. The units of the earlier tree are never removed.\n\nExpected: one gate run builds `camcraft-app` once (or once for each real profile), and a new tree replaces the units of the earlier tree, or the gate removes them.\n\nWork:\n1. Find what gives `camcraft-app` hundreds of different unit hashes in ONE gate run (for example one unit for each test binary or lane, a different `--target-dir` or build-dir, a per-step env, `--message-format`, or the `-p` sets of the steps).\n2. Fix it so one run builds `camcraft-app` the fewest times, and add a gate step that removes the units of a tree that is no longer built.\n3. Add a test: two gate runs on two different trees leave the unit count bounded.\n",
